shade: sample type 1 shadings on a coarser grid, refined at jumps

Function-based shadings were sampled on a 257x257 grid at load (66K
function calls each) and drawn as 65K quads regardless of their device
size. Edge-printed pages with a dozen small PostScript-function shadings
took 200-700 ms per page (#6402). Sample a 65x65 grid, then halve the
cells (up to 6 times) between neighbouring rows or columns whose colors
jump: those shadings are black outside the painted area and a coarse
cell smeared the black over its edge. The grid lines are no longer
evenly spaced, so fz_shade stores their positions (u.f.xs / u.f.ys).
When drawing, skip lines closer than ~2 device pixels.
